  "result": "`satisfies(version, range)` is now implemented in `src/semver.js` to follow `docs/SPEC.md`, and `npm test` passes (5 tests, 0 failed).\n\n**What it handles**\n- **Versions:** the strict version format and ordering from the spec, including prerelease ordering and ignored build metadata.\n- **Ranges:** `||` sets, comparators, x-ranges and partial versions, tilde, caret and hyphen ranges.\n- **Prerelease rule:** a prerelease version only matches a set that has a prerelease comparator on the same `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`.\n- **Invalid input:** an invalid version, an invalid range or a non-string argument returns `false` and never throws.\n\n**Tests:** `test/semver.test.js` covers matches, non-matches, invalid inputs and the full prerelease ordering chain.\n\n**Where the spec was silent, I chose:**\n- `>*` and `<*` match nothing, while `>=*` and `<=*` match any non-prerelease version.\n- An empty set in `a || || b` counts as \"any\", since the spec says an empty range means any version.\n- Whitespace is also allowed after `~` and `^`, not just after the comparison operators.\n- Prerelease identifiers that are numbers with leading zeros are accepted, because the spec only bans leading zeros in `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`.\n\nWhen I reread `test/semver.test.js` at the end it looked as intended, and the final run passed after my last edit to it.",
